(* Each object carries a certificate: the interfaces its module provides
   and the ones it was proved against, with their hashes (docs/abi.md).
   `pia-cert check` refuses objects proved against an interface that no
   object provides, or that another object provides differently.
// RUN: piac --emit=interface -o %t %S/Inputs/pixels.pia
// RUN: piac --emit=obj -o %t/pixels.o %S/Inputs/pixels.pia
// RUN: piac --emit=obj -o %t/blend.o --iface-path=%t %S/Inputs/blend.pia
// RUN: pia-cert dump %t/blend.o | FileCheck --check-prefix=DUMP %s
// RUN: pia-cert dump %t/pixels.o | FileCheck --check-prefix=LIB %s
// RUN: pia-cert check %t/pixels.o %t/blend.o | FileCheck --check-prefix=OK %s
// RUN: not pia-cert check %t/blend.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=MISSING %s
// RUN: piac --version | FileCheck --check-prefix=VERSION %s

   Advisories (ADR 0073) revoke proofs from a faulty piac or solver. The
   ones compiled in are listed; a newer set is added with --advisories. The
   first test advisory revokes these objects until Image.Pixels and Blend
   are accepted by name, which makes each a trusted item; the second names
   an engine their certificates do not, so it revokes neither. piac here is
   unstamped, which --require-released refuses.
// RUN: pia-cert advisories | FileCheck --check-prefix=LIST %s
// RUN: not pia-cert check --advisories=%S/Inputs/advisories %t/pixels.o %t/blend.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=REVOKED %s
// RUN: pia-cert check --advisories=%S/Inputs/advisories --accept-advisory=PIA-2099-0001:Image.Pixels --accept-advisory=PIA-2099-0001:Blend %t/pixels.o %t/blend.o | FileCheck --check-prefix=ACCEPTED %s
// RUN: not pia-cert check --require-released %t/pixels.o %t/blend.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=RELEASED %s

   piac checks itself against the advisories too: --version lists those
   that revoke it or its z3, and a run warns. A cache entry is keyed by
   z3's version, so with z3 revoked every entry it could read came from
   it, and the proof cache is neither read nor written.
// RUN: piac --version --advisories=%S/Inputs/advisories | FileCheck --check-prefix=SELF %s
// RUN: piac --verify --advisories=%S/Inputs/advisories --proof-cache=%t/cache %S/Inputs/pixels.pia 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOCACHE %s
// RUN: test ! -e %t/cache

   Image.Pixels again, with a stronger precondition on luma: Blend was
   proved against the old interface, so it must be proved again.
// RUN: mkdir %t/v2
// RUN: sed 's/r <= 250/r <= 240/' %S/Inputs/pixels.pia > %t/v2/pixels.pia
// RUN: piac --emit=obj -o %t/v2/pixels.o %t/v2/pixels.pia
// RUN: not pia-cert check %t/v2/pixels.o %t/blend.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=STALE %s

// DUMP: module Blend
// DUMP-NEXT: abi 1 {{[a-z0-9_]+-[a-z0-9_.-]+}}
// DUMP-NEXT: prover piac dev
// DUMP-NEXT: solver z3 {{[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+}}
// DUMP-NEXT: engines {{[a-z0-9:,.-]+}}
// DUMP-NEXT: provides Blend.C [[C:[0-9a-f]{64}]]
// DUMP-NEXT: requires Image.Pixels.Ops [[OPS:[0-9a-f]{64}]]

// LIB: module Image.Pixels
// LIB-DAG: provides Image.Pixels.Ops {{[0-9a-f]+}}
// LIB-DAG: provides Image.Pixels.C {{[0-9a-f]+}}

// OK: pia-cert: 2 objects link

// VERSION: piac dev
// VERSION-NEXT: Pia ABI 1
// VERSION-NEXT: z3 {{[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+}}

// LIST: PIA-2026-0001 unsound
// LIST-NEXT: Termination was checked only for direct recursion
// LIST-NEXT: piac 0.0.0+0 to 0.0.0+720

// REVOKED: '{{.*}}pixels.o': Image.Pixels was proved with z3 {{[0-9.]+}}, which PIA-2099-0001 revokes (Every z3 proves anything): rebuild it with a piac that fixes it (https://example.invalid/fix), or accept it with --accept-advisory=PIA-2099-0001:Image.Pixels
// REVOKED: '{{.*}}blend.o': Blend was proved with z3
// REVOKED-NOT: PIA-2099-0002

// ACCEPTED: pia-cert: trusted advisory PIA-2099-0001 Image.Pixels
// ACCEPTED-NEXT: pia-cert: trusted advisory PIA-2099-0001 Blend
// ACCEPTED-NEXT: pia-cert: 2 objects link

// RELEASED: '{{.*}}pixels.o' was built by an unstamped piac (dev), and --require-released refuses those

// SELF: z3 {{[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+}}
// SELF-NEXT: revoked by PIA-2099-0001: Every z3 proves anything
// SELF-NEXT: revoked by PIA-2099-0002: The fake engine proves anything

// NOCACHE: piac: warning: PIA-2099-0001 revokes this piac (dev) or its z3 ({{[0-9.]+}}): Every z3 proves anything; pia-cert will refuse what it proves
// NOCACHE: piac: warning: the proof cache is not used, since an advisory revokes z3

// MISSING: '{{.*}}blend.o' imports 'Image.Pixels.Ops', which no object provides

// STALE: '{{.*}}blend.o' was proved against 'Image.Pixels.Ops' {{[0-9a-f]+}}..., but '{{.*}}v2/pixels.o' provides {{[0-9a-f]+}}...: the interface changed
*)
